', 'what-is-artistic-swimming', 'Everything You Need to Know About This Amazing Sport', '<p>If you''ve stumbled across a video of athletes spinning upside down in a pool, launching each other into the air, and moving in perfect unison to music — and thought, <em>what is that?</em> — you''re in the right place.</p><p>Artistic swimming is one of the most physically demanding and visually stunning sports in the world. And yet, most people still know very little about it. Here''s your complete beginner''s guide.</p><hr><h3>A Sport With a New Name</h3><p>You might know this sport as synchronized swimming. That name stuck around for decades, and many people still use it today. But in 2017, the international governing body for aquatic sports — FINA — officially renamed it <strong>artistic swimming</strong>.</p><p>The new name was chosen intentionally. Yes, synchronization matters. But the sport is so much more than that. It''s about artistry, creativity, storytelling through movement, and athletic expression. "Artistic swimming" captures that bigger picture.</p><hr><h3>So What Actually Is Artistic Swimming?</h3><p>At its core, artistic swimming is a sport that combines <strong>swimming, dance, and gymnastics</strong> — all performed in the water, set to music.</p><p>Athletes choreograph routines that include spins, lifts, patterns, and formations. Every movement is timed to the music and coordinated with teammates. Judges score routines on both <strong>technical skill</strong> and <strong>artistic impression</strong>, which means the sport rewards creativity just as much as precision.</p><p>Think of it like figure skating or gymnastics — but in the water, with the added challenge of needing to tread water, hold your breath, and stay in sync with a team, all at the same time.</p><hr><h3>What Makes It So Physically Demanding?</h3><p>Artistic swimming looks graceful and effortless from the outside. That''s actually part of the skill. Beneath the surface, athletes are working incredibly hard.</p><p>Swimmers use a technique called the <strong>eggbeater kick</strong> to keep themselves elevated in the water — sometimes while lifting a teammate completely above the surface. They perform inverted positions, hold their breath for extended periods, and execute precise movements with their arms through a technique called <strong>sculling</strong>. Competitive routines can last five minutes, with athletes spending more than three of those minutes submerged.</p><p>The training behind it involves far more than pool time. Artistic swimmers also train in dance, gymnastics, strength conditioning, and aerobics. It''s a full-body, full-mind sport.</p><hr><h3>Is It Only for Elite Athletes?</h3><p>Not at all — and this is one of the best things about artistic swimming. The sport genuinely welcomes <strong>all ages and all skill levels</strong>.</p><p>Younger kids and beginners can start by learning basic water skills, simple choreography, and the fundamentals of moving as a team. From there, the progression goes as far as an athlete wants to take it — all the way up to local competitions, national teams, and the Olympics.</p><p>What makes artistic swimming special is that it meets kids where they are. Whether a child is a natural in the water or still building confidence, there''s a place for them in this sport.</p><hr><h3>What Values Does Artistic Swimming Build?</h3><p>Beyond the physical fitness, artistic swimming develops a set of life skills that parents consistently rave about.</p><p><strong>Teamwork</strong> is central to everything — a routine only works when every swimmer is committed to the group. <strong>Discipline</strong> comes naturally through the repetition required to perfect timing and technique. And because routines are performances with music, costumes, and expression, the sport builds <strong>confidence and self-expression</strong> in a way few other activities can.</p><p>Many athletes who grew up in artistic swimming credit the sport with shaping how they carry themselves, work with others, and push through challenges.</p><hr><h3>Artistic Swimming in Seattle</h3><p>Seattle has a vibrant and growing artistic swimming community, and <strong>Seattle Synchro</strong> is proud to be part of it. We offer programs for kids at every stage — from first-timers who are just curious about the sport, to competitive swimmers ready to take their training to the next level.</p><p>If your child loves swimming, dancing, being part of a team, or just wants to try something completely unlike anything they''ve done before, artistic swimming in Seattle might be exactly what they''ve been looking for.</p>', 'https://hfyxcakixklryajpnszd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog/1778012670302-8t9byntqbgf.jpg', 'Seattle Synchro Team', NULL, '["artistic swimming","synchronized swimming Seattle","kids swimming Seattle","artistic swimming for kids","summer camp Seattle"]', 'What Is Artistic Swimming? | Seattle Synchro', 'Artistic swimming blends swimming, dance, and gymnastics into one incredible sport. Learn what it is and how kids in Seattle can get started today!', 3, 1, '2026-05-05T20:12:10.781+00:00', '2026-05-05T20:12:11.388168+00:00', '2026-05-05T20:24:37.831121+00:00');
